# Copy to .env and fill in. Vite only exposes variables that start with VITE_.
VITE_ATS_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Not Vite's: scripts/corpus.ts reads a GitHub token for the corpus from its environment, never
# from this file, when gh is not logged in, as in CI. Never give either the VITE_ prefix.
# GH_TOKEN=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Not Vite's either: `corpus name --model` reads the naming model's key from its environment, never
# from this file, and asks the model only when given that flag, never in CI. The second name is
# the provider's own for the same key, one line with no spaces. NAMING_MODEL picks the model by its
# id, gemini-3.8-flash when unset, whose answers go in .corpus/cache/<id>/. Never give any of them
# the VITE_ prefix, which would put the key in the page.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# NAMING_MODEL=

# Not Vite's either, though read from this file: the dev server's naming route, /v1/name
# (scripts/serve-naming.ts), reads NAMING_API_KEY here, on the server side alone, and asks the
# naming model for what its cache does not hold. GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY, above, is read when
# it is unset, and NAMING_MODEL picks the model, here as for the runner. With neither key the route
# serves the cache alone, and the dev server says so when it starts. The Pages Function reads the
# same names from its own environment (functions/README.md). Never give it the VITE_ prefix, which
# would put the key in the page.
# NAMING_API_KEY=
